{
  "name": "a_face_beyond_the_largest_sixty_is_named_by_selector",
  "family": "measurement",
  "red_before": "0.153.0",
  "why": "FACES BEYOND THE 60 LARGEST (W3.1-bis.12). The state lists the 60 largest faces and says `truncated`; the selectors of a plan (@face(...)) are resolved against that list, so a small face of a part with more of them was «not found» although it was there. On the tube stand of task 07 (177 faces) the walls of the third and the fourth foot tie at 4,800 mm2 behind 40 larger faces of the frame, and the plan of the D9 prerequisite stopped at its first gusset. This case is the smallest part that has the defect: a plate 200 x 100 x 10 with 64 holes of M6 (two features of 32: the wizard makes at most 60 in one) (Ø6.6 by the ISO table) and ONE hole of Ø3, so 70 or 71 faces, and the wall of the Ø3 hole is the SMALLEST face of the part (area pi x 3 x 10 = 94 mm2 against pi x 6.6 x 10 = 207 mm2 of every other wall): beyond the 60 largest by construction, not by the luck of the order of the ties.",
  "defect_caught": "A face that is not among the 60 largest cannot be named by a selector, and so cannot be measured, drilled, filleted or reinforced. Red on a library older than 0.153.0 because the selector «@face(diameter_mm~=3)» finds nothing in the list of 60 (the step cannot be built: the bench says so and the case is red); green after, because the reader of selectors reads every face of the part and the library numbers a face it did not list by its rank.",
  "_why_the_numbers": "The small hole is at x = 90, y = 0 and the side of the plate at x = 100: the wall of a Ø3 hole is 1.5 from its axis, so the shortest distance from the wall to the side is 100 - 90 - 1.5 = 8.5 mm. The 64 holes are on x = -70..70 (pitch 20) and y = -42..42 (pitch 12), so the nearest one ends at x = 73.3, 16.7 mm from the small one: nothing is in the way, and no hole touches another or the border (the hole of the wizard refuses a distance below the radius, and the case would say so at step 2).",
  "_the_premise_is_checked": "state.faces_total is read after the holes: it exists only when the part has MORE faces than the state lists, so the case says by itself that it is on the defect and not beside it. If it is red there, the plate is wrong and the selector is not to blame.",
